/* oracle-text.js — classic script; assigns to window.TD. No ES modules, so file:// works.
   Longer texts for oracle.html: rune:<id> (upright, in depth), runerev:<id> (reversed), dice:p:<Planet>, dice:s:<Sign>,
   dice:h:<N> (astro dice). 290 texts. Written fresh for this demo; a live site edits or replaces them.
   Built by ../_astro-corpus-work/oracle/build-oracle.js. */
window.TD = window.TD || {};
window.TD.ORACLE_TEXT = {"rune:fehu":"Cattle were once the thing a household could count, move and trade, and the rune carries that picture of resources in motion. For your question, it suggests that what you have, whether time, skill, money or goodwill, does its best work when it circulates. Think of the colleague who shares contacts freely and finds that help comes back around, while the one who guards everything sits on a small pile. Ask what you are holding that could be put to use, and what effort deserves a fair return. In modern rune reading, Fehu opens the Elder Futhark and speaks of value that stays alive because it keeps moving.",
"rune:uruz":"The aurochs was a huge wild ox, larger than any farm bull, and the rune borrows its untamed power. For the situation you are asking about, it points to raw strength that has not yet been given a direction: stamina, nerve and a stubborn will to keep going. Picture someone who finally says the hard thing in a meeting, or who gets up for a morning run in the cold. The strength is real, but it needs a harness, or it simply stampedes. Channel it into one clear task rather than scattering it. Rest counts too, since a strong animal that never recovers wears down.",
"rune:thurisaz":"A thorn on a hedge does two jobs: it keeps trouble out and it pricks anyone who grabs carelessly. Thurisaz carries both edges, and in modern rune reading it is linked with giants and with raw, defensive force. For your question, it suggests a point of friction you cannot walk around, perhaps a boundary being tested or a decision that has to be faced directly. An everyday case is the awkward conversation you have been rehearsing for weeks. Pause before reacting, because force used in haste cuts the user as well. Choose what you are defending, then act with calm and clear intent.",
"rune:ansuz":"Breath, speech and a divine voice sit behind this rune, which many readers tie to the spoken word and to inspiration. For your question, it suggests that communication is central right now: a message, a piece of advice, or a phrase you have been trying to find. The helpful friend who says exactly what you needed to hear is a good picture of it. Listen more than you usually do, and notice what repeats. Your own words also carry weight at the moment, so say them plainly and honestly. Written notes, a call you have put off, or a teacher worth asking could all be useful channels.",
"rune:raidho":"Riding a road is the image here: a rider, a horse, and a route that has to be covered at a sensible pace. Your question may involve a literal trip, but just as often it points to a path of work or growth that goes best in good order. Think of a road journey where someone plans the stops, checks the map and keeps the pace steady instead of racing. Right rhythm matters more than speed. Ask whether you are heading the right way, and whether your preparations match the distance. In modern rune reading, Raidho favours movement that is deliberate and well timed.",
"rune:kenaz":"A torch held up in a dark hall shows what was always there. Kenaz is the rune of that light, and also of the craftsperson's fire that shapes raw material into something useful. For your question, it suggests that clarity is within reach: a muddle begins to sort itself, or a skill you have built can finally be applied. Picture the moment a tangled spreadsheet or a messy draft suddenly makes sense. Follow the insight while it is bright and give it a form, whether a plan, a sketch or a first page. Keep the flame fed with practice, and do not burn anyone with it.",
"rune:gebo":"A gift in old Germanic life was never really free, since it created a bond and an expectation that the favour would be returned. Gebo, drawn as a simple crossing, speaks of that balanced exchange. For your question, it suggests that the situation works best as a two-way arrangement where both sides give and both sides receive. The neighbour who lends a ladder and later borrows a drill is a good example. Look at whether the give and take is fair, and whether you are comfortable receiving as well as offering. Generosity with no expectation of anything back can also be a quiet strength.",
"rune:wunjo":"Joy in this rune is the settled kind: the relief of a table full of familiar faces, or the ease after a hard stretch ends. Wunjo is often described as belonging and contentment, with things falling into place without strain. For your question, it suggests that the situation tends toward harmony when you stop forcing it, and that shared good feeling is worth noticing. An example is the team that finishes a project and actually enjoys the evening together. Let yourself take it in rather than rushing to the next worry. Pass some of it along, because joy kept to yourself grows thin.",
"rune:hagalaz":"Hail falls out of a clear-looking sky, flattens a crop in minutes, and then melts into water that feeds the soil. Hagalaz carries that harsh, sudden quality: disruption you did not choose and could not plan for. For your question, it suggests that something may be shaken loose, such as a plan, an assumption or a comfortable routine. Imagine a schedule thrown out by a last-minute change. The useful response is to protect what matters most and stop clinging to what is already scattered. Afterward, look at what is still standing. That is usually what was sound all along.",
"rune:naudiz":"Need is the stark word here, and in the old tradition it also names the fire made by friction, the hard-won spark. Naudiz points to constraint, a lack, a squeeze that is hard to enjoy but teaches a great deal. For your question, it suggests the situation is asking you to separate what you merely want from what you truly require. Picture trimming a budget of hours rather than money, and finding two or three things you cannot give up. Patience helps, and so does asking for modest support. Pressure this tight often reveals a real priority that comfort had hidden.",
"rune:isa":"Ice is a single vertical line, plain and cold, and the rune is about things holding still. For your question, it suggests a standstill: a conversation gone quiet, a plan on pause, a feeling you cannot quite thaw. Think of a pond frozen over in January, where nothing visible moves and yet nothing is lost. The advice is to keep your shape and resist the urge to smash through. Use the pause for rest, tidying up and thinking. Ice also preserves, so protect what you value. In modern rune reading, the thaw comes on its own schedule, and pushing it rarely helps.",
"rune:jera":"A year turning is the picture, with the long wait of seed, weather and tending, and then the reaping. Jera is the rune of the cycle, and it suggests that the situation follows its own seasons. For your question, it points to the idea that steady effort has a delayed payoff, much like a garden planted in spring that gives nothing in April. If you have been consistent, the results may be closer than they feel. If you have not started, the season is simply still open. Do the next sensible task, avoid hurrying what cannot be hurried, and let time do its share.",
"rune:eihwaz":"The yew is an evergreen that lives for centuries, keeping its needles through every winter, and the rune is tied to that stubborn endurance. For your question, it suggests that the situation is more about lasting than winning. Picture a person who goes through a long reorganization at work, bends when needed and still stays recognizably themselves. Strength here is flexible rather than rigid. Ask what in you stays steady when everything else is being rearranged. Draw on that, and let the rest change. In modern rune reading, Eihwaz also hints at the link between ending and renewal, so a close may not be a loss.",
"rune:perthro":"Nobody agrees on what this rune originally named, though many readers picture a cup used to cast lots. That uncertainty suits it: Perthro stands for chance, mystery and things not yet shown. For your question, it suggests that part of the answer is hidden, and no amount of worrying will pull it into view early. Think of waiting for a message you cannot hurry, or a decision that depends on other people. Do what is within your hands, then loosen your grip. Curiosity serves better than certainty here. Trust the process enough to stay open to a result you did not predict.",
"rune:algiz":"Spread fingers, or the antlers of an elk, make the shape of this rune, and it is often read as a sign of guarding and reaching toward something higher. For your question, it suggests that you have more protection than you feel, whether from people around you, your own instincts or simple good sense. A friend who calls to check in just when you needed it is a fair example. Pay attention to the quiet inner alarm that says yes or no. Keep your boundaries clear and kind. Asking for backing when you need it is not weakness but part of how the shield works.",
"rune:sowilo":"The sun is the brightest thing overhead, and this rune is read as light, vitality and a clear line of travel. For your question, it suggests that energy is available and direction is easier to see than it has been. Picture the lift in a morning when you finally know which task comes first. Confidence is worth using now, but brightness can also glare, so do not let it blind you to details or to other people in the room. Aim the light at one honest goal. In modern rune reading, Sowilo supports success that comes from clarity and warmth together.",
"rune:tiwaz":"Tyr, the god tied to this arrow-shaped rune, is remembered in Norse stories for putting word and honour ahead of personal comfort. Tiwaz carries that idea of justice, duty and courage with a cost. For your question, it suggests that the situation calls for fairness and a clear moral line. An example is speaking up for a colleague who is being talked over, though it makes the room tense. Check that your aim is true before you let fly. Act from principle rather than from pride, and be ready to accept some discomfort for the sake of doing right.",
"rune:berkano":"Birch is among the first trees to green in spring, and its soft, pale branches have long stood for fresh starts. Berkano is read as growth, nurture and the care that a young thing needs. For your question, it suggests that something small is beginning, perhaps a project, a habit, a friendship or a plan, and it will not thrive on neglect or on rough handling. Think of tending a seedling: water, light and patience beat pressure. Offer gentle, regular attention. Protect it from early criticism, including your own. Family and home life may also be part of the picture.",
"rune:ehwaz":"A horse and its rider only get anywhere when each trusts the other, and the rune carries that picture of two parties moving as one. For your question, it suggests that progress comes through partnership, loyalty and steady cooperation rather than solo effort. Think of two people who have worked together for years and finish each other's tasks without discussion. Check whether your trust is well placed and whether you are carrying your share of the reins. Move at a pace the pair can sustain. In modern rune reading, Ehwaz also speaks of gradual, reliable advance, the kind that does not need dramatic gestures.",
"rune:mannaz":"The name means a human being, and the rune pictures two figures reaching toward each other, so it is about the self set among other people. For your question, it suggests that the answer lies partly in who you ask and how well you know your own mind. Imagine a hard choice that clears up after one honest talk with a trusted friend. Cooperation helps now, and so does self-honesty about your strengths and limits. Offer your help as freely as you accept it. Where you feel alone with the matter, reaching out is probably more useful than waiting for clarity to arrive.",
"rune:laguz":"Water takes the shape of whatever holds it, and it keeps finding the low route to the sea. Laguz is the rune of that flowing, feeling side of life, linked in modern reading with intuition and the unseen. For your question, it suggests that your emotions carry real information about the situation, even if they are hard to put into words. Think of the gut sense that a room is tense before anyone speaks. Do not force the current. Let your feelings be named, then act on them gently. Depth can also drown, so keep a firm bank, such as a routine or a trusted person, nearby.",
"rune:ingwaz":"Ing is a god of fertility in Germanic tradition, and the rune is often drawn as a seed or a closed shape holding something in. Ingwaz suggests completion and quiet potential at the same moment. For your question, it points to a phase that is ready to be finished, a chapter closed properly, with the next one resting out of sight. Think of tidying the last loose ends of a project before a holiday. Finish what is nearly done, then give yourself a real pause. Nothing has to be planted in a hurry. Rest gathers strength for what grows next.",
"rune:dagaz":"Dawn is the moment when the sky changes from dark to light, and no one can say exactly when it happened. Dagaz carries that image of daybreak and of a turning that changes how everything looks. For your question, it suggests that a new outlook is available, perhaps after a long stretch of confusion or waiting. Picture waking after a bad night and seeing the same problem in a calmer, wider light. Let the shift in view happen, and be ready to act from it. Do not cling to the old frame. In modern rune reading, Dagaz often marks a breakthrough in awareness more than in events.",
"rune:othala":"An estate passed down through a family is the old picture: land, a house, a name, and the duties that go with them. Othala is read as home, heritage and what you inherit, whether property, habits, stories or values. For your question, it suggests the situation touches your roots and your sense of belonging. An example is a family recipe or custom you realize you want to keep, or one you want to leave behind. Ask what you have received that is worth carrying forward, and what no longer fits. Lasting value comes from the ties you tend, not only from what is handed over.",
"runerev:fehu":"Cattle that wander off the pasture are still cattle, but nobody is minding them. Reversed, this rune points to value leaking out through small, unnoticed gaps: money lent without a clear understanding, hours given to people who never return the favor, energy spent on things you do not care about. Look at where your resources actually go this month. A quiet audit of what you give out, and to whom, tends to help more than any grand fix.",
"runerev:uruz":"A wild ox pulling too long without water turns sluggish and short-tempered. Reversed, this rune suggests strength that is misused or running low: pushing through exhaustion, forcing a door that needs a slower approach, or doubting your own stamina. Think of the person who keeps saying yes to extra shifts until everything feels heavy. In your question, patience may do what pressure cannot. Rest first, then pick the one task that truly needs your force.",
"runerev:thurisaz":"A thorn catches the sleeve of anyone who hurries past. Reversed, this rune suggests a sharp reaction that may be regretted: the reply typed in anger, the door slammed over a small insult, the old grudge swinging at a new target. It is a warning about haste and spite, not about fate. If your question involves conflict, pause before you strike. A night's sleep and a glass of water often change what the right answer looks like.",
"runerev:ansuz":"Breath carries a word, and a word can be bent on the way. Reversed, this rune suggests mixed messages, half-heard instructions, or someone shading the truth, possibly you. Picture a group chat where three people each understood a different plan. Check what you have been told and where it came from. Then say what you mean in plain terms, even if it feels blunt. Clear speech is what helps here, and it costs little.",
"runerev:raidho":"The road is still there, but the wheel has caught on something. Reversed, this rune suggests delays, a plan with a bad fit, or a trip that goes sideways because nobody checked the route. It can be a literal journey or a project that keeps stalling at the same step. Resist the urge to rush onward just to feel movement. Rethink the route, confirm the details, and make sure everyone involved is heading the same direction.",
"runerev:kenaz":"A torch gutters, and for a while the room is dim. Reversed, this rune suggests a creative block, a loss of clarity, or a skill that feels temporarily out of reach. Think of the writer staring at a blank page, or the person who cannot see their next step in a job. The light is not gone for good. Do not force it with panic. Keep the small habits going, and give the flame time to catch again.",
"runerev:wunjo":"A feast is happening, and you are standing outside the window. Reversed, this rune suggests joy that is delayed, a feeling of being on the edge of the group, or contentment that keeps slipping out of reach. It may show up as comparing your life to everyone else's highlights. In your question, the helpful move is small and active: message the person who matters, join the plain ordinary gathering, and let belonging be built rather than awaited.",
"runerev:perthro":"A lot cup sits closed, and nobody wants to look inside. Reversed, this rune suggests secrets, stagnation, and a situation where something important is being kept out of sight, by others or by you. Think of the bill left unopened on the counter, or the conversation everyone is circling. Chance is not the issue here, avoidance is. Bring the hidden piece into the open, ask the direct question, and see what shifts once it is on the table.",
"runerev:algiz":"An elk's antlers spread wide as a guard, but a lowered head leaves the flanks exposed. Reversed, this rune suggests thin defences: being too trusting, ignoring a gut feeling, or leaving a boundary unstated. Picture someone who lends their password to be polite. In your question, look at whom you let close and what you leave unguarded. Protecting what is yours is not coldness. A clear limit, calmly stated, is a form of care.",
"runerev:tiwaz":"A spear thrown without aim hits nothing worth having. Reversed, this rune suggests scattered energy, a fight that is not worth fighting, or a sense of justice that has tipped into stubbornness. Think of the long argument over who was right when the real issue was something else. Check your motives honestly: is this about the principle or about winning? Put your effort into the one cause that deserves it and let the rest go.",
"runerev:berkano":"A birch sapling bends but stays rooted, and when the roots are neglected the branches stop reaching. Reversed, this rune suggests stalled growth and worry about home, family, or the people who keep you steady. It might be a household strain that no one has named, or a project that cannot start because the foundations feel shaky. Tend the roots first. Small acts of care, like a phone call or a tidied room, give new growth somewhere to begin.",
"runerev:ehwaz":"Two horses pulling in different tempos make a wagon lurch. Reversed, this rune suggests restlessness, a partnership that is out of step, or a change made too quickly for others to follow. Think of the couple or coworkers who want the same thing yet keep talking over each other. In your question, slow down and listen for the rhythm the other side is using. Matching pace is often more useful than choosing the faster road.",
"runerev:mannaz":"A person looks into a pond and sees only a reflection of what they expect. Reversed, this rune suggests isolation, self-deception, or a gap between how you see yourself and how others do. It may feel like nobody understands you, or like you have stopped noticing your own part in things. Take an honest look at yourself, perhaps with a trusted friend as a mirror. Then reach out. Connection is both the sore spot and the way through here.",
"runerev:laguz":"Water that has no banks spreads into a marsh, and every step sinks a little. Reversed, this rune suggests confusion, murky feelings, and judgement clouded by mood or wishful thinking. Think of making a decision at midnight when worry has turned a small problem into an ocean. In your question, do not drift. Find solid ground: write the facts down, talk with someone steady, and leave the big choices until the water has settled.",
"runerev:othala":"An old family house can shelter you or keep you from leaving. Reversed, this rune suggests clinging to the past, friction over inheritance of any kind, or traditions that no longer fit who you have become. It might be a habit handed down, a role you were given in the family, or a place you keep for sentiment alone. Ask what truly belongs to you now. Keep the gifts, put down the weight, and build a home of your own choosing.",
"dice:p:Sun":"Your sense of who you are sits at the center of the question. The situation asks what you actually want, not what looks good to others. Think of the moment you stop explaining yourself and simply say what matters to you. Vitality and purpose both point the same way: act from your own core.",
"dice:p:Moon":"Feelings and needs are steering the question, often quietly. The situation may be asking what makes you feel safe, fed and at home. Notice your habitual reaction before you decide anything, like the way you reach for a snack or a blanket when stress hits. Honoring a real need usually clears the air.",
"dice:p:Mercury":"Words, thinking and information are the working parts here. The situation responds to clear talk, careful reading and honest negotiation. Think of the email you keep rewriting or the fine print you skimmed. Say it plainly, ask the follow-up question, and write down what was agreed so nobody has to guess later.",
"dice:p:Venus":"Affection, pleasure and what you value are at work in your question. The situation asks what you find worth caring about and what feels harmonious rather than forced. It can show up as taste, as warmth toward someone, or as how you treat your own resources. Choose what feels both kind and genuinely appealing.",
"dice:p:Mars":"Drive and the urge to act are powering the question. The situation may involve friction, a stalled start, or energy that wants a target. Picture the gym session or the blunt conversation you keep postponing. Move on purpose rather than in a flash of irritation, and pick one clear step to take.",
"dice:p:Jupiter":"Growth and openness are the themes tied to your question. The situation invites a wider view, a bit of faith and some generosity. Think of saying yes to the class, the introduction or the longer road. Enthusiasm helps, though it can stretch things too far, so keep a sense of proportion.",
"dice:p:Saturn":"Limits, time and responsibility shape the question. The situation rewards patience and honest effort over shortcuts, like the skill that only improves with steady practice. A boundary or a deadline may feel heavy, yet it gives the thing a frame. Ask what a reliable version of you would do next.",
"dice:p:Uranus":"Surprise and a need for freedom are stirring your question. The situation may not follow the script, and part of you wants room to do it differently. Think of the sudden idea in the shower that rearranges your plans. Stay flexible, and test the new approach on a small scale first.",
"dice:p:Neptune":"Intuition, dreams and a certain fog are present in your question. The situation may hold more than the facts show, and clarity may come slowly. Picture a half-remembered dream that colors your morning. Trust your sensitivity, but check details with someone grounded, and give yourself time before locking anything in.",
"dice:p:Pluto":"Depth and hidden power are moving beneath your question. The situation may be asking for something to be let go so that something truer can take its place. Think of clearing out a closet you have avoided for years. Look honestly at what drives you, and go slowly through the hard parts.",
"dice:p:NorthNode":"The direction of growth is what your question touches. The situation points toward something unfamiliar that stretches you, even if it feels awkward at first. Think of signing up for the thing that makes you a beginner again. Comfort is not the guide here, so lean gently toward what feels like a larger version of your path.",
"dice:p:SouthNode":"Old habits and familiar ground are at work in your question. The situation may be pulling you toward what you already do well, which is comforting and also a little worn. Think of the reflex answer you give without thinking. Appreciate what the past taught you, then loosen your grip on what no longer fits.",
"dice:s:Aries":"Directness is the style of the unfolding. The situation moves best through a quick, honest first step rather than long deliberation. Think of walking up and asking instead of hinting. Boldness opens doors, though pausing for one breath before acting keeps enthusiasm from running past the people involved in your question.",
"dice:s:Taurus":"Patience sets the pace here. The situation unfolds slowly and rewards practical, steady choices, like building a habit one dull but dependable day at a time. Resist the push to rush it. Stubbornness can creep in, so ask whether you are being steady or simply refusing to move on your question.",
"dice:s:Gemini":"Conversation is the route through. The situation develops by asking, listening, comparing notes and staying open to a second opinion. Think of the idea that improves after you talk it over with a friend. Variety helps, though scattered attention can thin things out, so choose one thread and follow it a while.",
"dice:s:Cancer":"Care and protectiveness color how this unfolds. The situation moves through feelings, and people respond to warmth more than to argument. Think of cooking for someone who is having a rough week. Looking after what matters is a strength, while retreating into your shell is the thing to watch in your question.",
"dice:s:Leo":"Openness and generosity shape the way things come out. The situation responds to sincere warmth and a willingness to be seen, like sharing your work before it feels perfect. Let your heart show. Pride is the thing to mind, so give others their share of the spotlight and credit where it is due.",
"dice:s:Virgo":"Care for detail guides the unfolding. The situation improves through small, useful adjustments, like fixing the one broken step in a routine instead of overhauling everything. Be practical and precise. Worry and fault-finding can take over, so aim for helpful rather than flawless as you work through your question.",
"dice:s:Libra":"Fairness and cooperation set the tone. The situation moves best when you weigh both sides and look for a result that works for everyone involved, like two people trading small concessions. Diplomacy is your tool. Indecision is the snag, so let a gentle deadline help you settle on your question.",
"dice:s:Scorpio":"Intensity and privacy mark how this plays out. The situation runs deeper than it looks, and the real motives may stay beneath the surface for a while, like a conversation that only starts once everyone else has left. Go for truth over appearances. Guard against all-or-nothing thinking.",
"dice:s:Sagittarius":"Optimism and plain speaking shape the way forward. The situation opens up when you widen your view and say what you honestly think, like the friend who suggests the longer trip. Keep your faith in the bigger picture. Bluntness can sting, so check how your words land.",
"dice:s:Capricorn":"Discipline and patience carry the situation. It unfolds step by step, rewarding the person who shows up, plans and keeps a long view, like saving effort for a goal that is months away. Reserve and ambition are both useful. Allow some warmth and rest, since not everything about your question is a task.",
"dice:s:Aquarius":"An unconventional, independent streak shapes this. The situation may work best through fresh ideas and the support of a wider group, like a friend who sees the problem from outside. Stand back to get perspective. Detachment can turn into distance, so keep one honest line of contact open about your question.",
"dice:s:Pisces":"Softness and intuition guide the unfolding. The situation moves by feel more than by logic, with compassion doing work that argument cannot, like sensing a friend is upset before a word is said. Trust that sense. Boundaries can blur, so keep a little room that belongs only to you.",
"dice:h:1":"Your own self is the arena for this question: your body, your appearance and the way you begin things. The situation is personal, and it responds to how you present yourself and what you start. Think of a fresh haircut or a first day somewhere new. Begin with yourself, and let the rest follow.",
"dice:h:2":"Money, possessions and what you value are the setting for your question. The situation touches how you earn, spend and measure your own worth, like deciding what is truly worth keeping. Look at the practical side, such as a budget or a tool you rely on, and ask what you honestly consider valuable.",
"dice:h:3":"Everyday communication is where this plays out. The situation lives in conversations, messages, siblings, neighbors, short trips and learning, like the quick text or the errand that carries more weight than expected. Keep exchanges clear and curious. Small, regular contact in your daily surroundings matters more than a grand gesture for your question.",
"dice:h:4":"Home and family are the ground of your question. The situation is rooted in where you live, where you come from and the people closest to you, like the kitchen table where real talk happens. Look at what makes you feel settled. Strengthening your foundation helps whatever you build on it.",
"dice:h:5":"Play, romance and creative joy form the stage for this. The situation asks where you take pleasure and what you enjoy making, like a hobby done only because it delights you. Let lightness in. Giving yourself room to flirt, create or simply have fun clarifies what your question really wants.",
"dice:h:6":"Daily work and routine are where your question lands. The situation shows up in habits, tasks, schedules and how you look after yourself day to day, like the morning routine that quietly sets your mood. Small, useful improvements count. Tidy up one process, and see how the rest of your day responds.",
"dice:h:7":"Other people, especially close one-to-one partners, are the setting here. The situation involves a partner, a collaborator, a contract or an open rival, like a negotiation where both sides truly listen. Pay attention to what the other person needs. Mutual give and take brings more clarity than going it alone.",
"dice:h:8":"Shared resources and deep bonds are involved in your question. The situation touches intimacy, joint money, trust and the endings that make room for renewal, like finally closing a chapter you have held onto. Be honest about what is shared and what is private. Go gently, and speak plainly.",
"dice:h:9":"Far horizons are the territory here. The situation involves travel, study, beliefs and the search for meaning, including formal rules and bigger principles, like the course or trip that changes how you see things. Widen your perspective. Ask what you truly believe about this, and learn something new to test it.",
"dice:h:10":"Career and public standing frame this question. The situation connects to your goals, your reputation and the role others see you in, like the project that shows your skill. Think about the long climb rather than the next small step. Ask what you want to be known for, and act with that in mind.",
"dice:h:11":"Friends, groups and hopes are the backdrop. The situation plays out among communities, teams and shared causes, like the circle that lifts an idea you could not carry alone. Reach out and share your wishes. The people around you may offer a view you lack, so listen as much as you speak.",
"dice:h:12":"Quiet, hidden places hold your question. The situation sits in solitude, rest and the unconscious, the part of life that works behind the scenes, like the answer that arrives after a night's sleep. Step back and give yourself stillness. What you cannot yet see may need time away from noise.",
"vision:major-00:up":"A traveler in a bright patterned tunic stands at a cliff edge, a small white dog leaping at their heels and a white rose held loosely in one hand. The sky is wide open, and the first step looks light, curious and unafraid.",
"vision:major-00:rev":"The traveler hovers at the cliff edge, bundle on shoulder, looking at the sky instead of the ground. The little dog barks a warning that goes unheard. A step is coming, but it wants a glance downward first.",
"vision:major-01:up":"Behind a table of cup, coin, sword and wand, a figure in white and red raises one wand to the heavens and points the other hand to the earth. Roses and lilies bloom overhead. Everything needed is already laid out within reach.",
"vision:major-01:rev":"The table is still crowded with cup, coin, sword and wand, but the figure's raised arm wavers and the flowers droop a little. Skill is present, though it is scattered, or used for show rather than for the work at hand.",
"vision:major-02:up":"A calm figure in blue robes sits between a dark pillar and a pale one, a crescent at the feet and a half-hidden scroll held in the lap. A veil of pomegranates hangs behind. Nothing is said, and the silence is the message.",
"vision:major-02:rev":"The veil behind the seated woman hangs heavy and the scroll stays tucked away. Between the two pillars the air is thick with things unsaid. Something known inside is being ignored, or a secret is held too tightly.",
"vision:major-03:up":"A figure lounges on cushions in a golden wheat field, crowned with twelve points of light and wearing a gown patterned with pomegranates. A stream runs nearby and the forest sways behind. Abundance here is ripe and unhurried.",
"vision:major-03:rev":"The wheat stands in the field but the stream runs thin, and the figure on the cushions sits with a gaze turned inward. The garden is rich, yet it is being neglected, or smothered by too much giving and too little rest.",
"vision:major-04:up":"A bearded ruler sits on a throne of carved rock marked with rams' heads, armor beneath a red robe, an ankh in one hand and an orb in the other. Barren red mountains rise behind. Order is being built here, firm and steady.",
"vision:major-04:rev":"The rocky throne looks cold, and the ruler's grip on the orb is a little too tight. Behind the seat the mountains offer no shade. Structure is turning into rigidity, or a rule is enforced where a conversation would serve better.",
"vision:major-05:up":"A robed teacher in a red mantle sits between two gray pillars, one hand raised in blessing, two keys crossed below. Two kneeling followers listen. Here is a tradition, a trusted lineage, a known way of doing things.",
"vision:major-05:rev":"The raised hand of the teacher between the pillars stays rigid, and the crossed keys lie unused while the two followers glance toward the door. Old rules are being repeated without conviction. A personal way of doing it is asking to be heard.",
"vision:major-06:up":"Two figures stand unclothed in a green garden beneath a great winged presence in a bright sky. A tree of flame rises behind one, a tree of fruit with a coiled snake behind the other. They face each other, and a heartfelt choice is forming.",
"vision:major-06:rev":"The two figures in the garden stand apart, looking away from each other and from the winged presence above. The trees behind them sway unattended. A choice is being avoided, or two halves are out of tune with what each really wants.",
"vision:major-07:up":"An armored figure stands upright in a chariot of pale rock beneath a canopy of light, a black sphinx and a white sphinx at rest in front. A walled city lies behind. Will and focus hold two opposing pulls and steer them forward.",
"vision:major-07:rev":"The two sphinxes pull in opposite directions and the figure in the cart grips an empty rein. The city behind is still in sight. Momentum is scattered, so slowing down and agreeing on a direction would serve better than force.",
"vision:major-08:up":"A figure in white with an infinity sign above the head gently closes the jaws of a lion, a flower garland looped around its neck. The animal softens at the touch. Quiet courage is winning, and patience is the real power.",
"vision:major-08:rev":"The figure in white fumbles with the lion's jaws, and the garland slips. The animal is restless and the calm is thin. Self-doubt or a loud temper is crowding out steady courage, and a few slow breaths would help.",
"vision:major-09:up":"On a snowy mountain peak at dusk, a gray-cloaked elder stands with a lantern held high, a staff in the other hand. Inside the lantern burns a six-pointed light. The way ahead is lit only a few steps at a time, and that is enough.",
"vision:major-09:rev":"The elder on the snowy peak has lowered the lantern, and the light flickers inside the cloak. Solitude has gone from restful to lonely, or the quiet is being used to hide from the path. A word with a trusted friend could help.",
"vision:major-10:up":"A great turning disc hangs in the clouds, carved with strange letters and ringed by winged beings reading from books in the four corners. A snake descends on one side, a jackal rises on the other. A turn is under way, and the pattern is larger than any single moment.",
"vision:major-10:rev":"The great disc in the clouds has slowed, and the jackal and snake seem to hold their places. The winged readers look up from their books. A cycle is stuck or repeating, and the way to move it is a small, deliberate change.",
"vision:major-11:up":"A crowned figure in red sits between two pillars with a sword raised in one hand and balanced scales in the other. A purple cloth hangs behind. Clear facts and fair weighing are asked for, and honest accounting settles the matter.",
"vision:major-11:rev":"The scales in the seated figure's hand tilt, and the sword wavers over a muddle of half-truths. The purple cloth hangs crooked. A decision is being made on poor information, or a fair look at one's own part is being put off.",
"vision:major-12:up":"A figure hangs by one foot from a living wooden frame, hands tucked behind the back, legs crossed, a soft halo of light around the head. The face is calm. A pause is being offered, and a new view comes from letting go of the old one.",
"vision:major-12:rev":"The figure on the wooden frame twists and tugs at the cord, the halo dim. The calm is gone and the waiting feels like a trap. A sacrifice is being made without purpose, so it may be time to ask what the pause is for.",
"vision:major-13:up":"A skeleton in black armor rides a white horse beneath a black banner marked with a white rose, while a king, a bishop, a maiden and a child face the rider. Far off, light rises between two pillars. An ending is making way for what comes after.",
"vision:major-13:rev":"The pale horse stands still and the rider's banner hangs limp. In the distance the light between the two pillars waits. Something finished is being held onto, and the change cannot begin until it is allowed to go.",
"vision:major-14:up":"A winged figure in white stands with one foot in a pool and one on the shore, pouring water between two cups in an unbroken stream. Irises grow nearby and a path leads to a glowing crown on the horizon. Patient blending brings balance.",
"vision:major-14:rev":"The water between the two cups splashes and misses. The winged figure at the pool's edge is pouring too fast, or too much of one thing. The path to the crown on the horizon is still there, but pace and proportion need a second look.",
"vision:major-15:up":"A horned, bat-winged creature squats on a black pedestal while a bare man and woman stand chained loosely at its feet, small horns on each. The chains are slack enough to lift off. A hold is at work here, and it can be loosened.",
"vision:major-15:rev":"The chains around the two figures at the pedestal have loosened and one has slipped from a neck. The horned creature above looks less sure. A habit or hold is weakening, and the first steps away are shaky but real.",
"vision:major-16:up":"Lightning strikes the crown of a tall spire on a rocky peak, flames bursting from its windows as two figures fall headlong into a dark sky. Sparks drift like falling lights. A shaky structure is giving way, and it clears room for something truer.",
"vision:major-16:rev":"The tall spire still stands, but cracks run through its walls and a dark sky presses close. The lightning has not yet come, or its force is being held back. A needed change is being resisted, and it may arrive anyway, so prepare gently.",
"vision:major-17:up":"A figure kneels at a quiet pool beneath a sky of eight gleaming points, one great light among them. Water pours from two jugs, one onto the land and one into the pool. A bird perches in a tree behind. Calm hope is flowing freely.",
"vision:major-17:rev":"The kneeling figure at the pool pours from two jugs, but the sky above is faint and the water barely ripples. The bird in the tree is hidden. Hope has grown thin, or has been tucked away, and a small act of faith can bring it back.",
"vision:major-18:up":"A full pale disc with a face glows between two pillars, while a dog and a wolf howl at it from a winding path and a crayfish crawls from a pond. Everything is half seen. The way forward is uncertain, and feelings may run stronger than facts.",
"vision:major-18:rev":"The pale disc between the two pillars dims, and the dog, wolf and crayfish settle down. The path ahead is slowly coming into view. A fog of worry is thinning, and what was feared is shrinking to its real size.",
"vision:major-19:up":"A great golden disc blazes in a clear sky above a wall of sunflowers, and a laughing child rides a white horse with a red banner streaming. Everything is warm and in the open. Joy and honest vitality are shining on your question.",
"vision:major-19:rev":"A pale golden disc shines through thin cloud over the sunflower wall, and the child on the white horse looks around with a smaller smile. The warmth is there but muted. Optimism needs a little rest, or a clearer look, before it shines fully.",
"vision:major-20:up":"A trumpet sounds from a cloud, and below it figures rise from their open boxes with arms lifted toward the light. Mountains stand cold behind them. Something long settled is being called awake, and your question may be asking you to answer.",
"vision:major-20:rev":"The trumpet is there, but its note comes muffled, and the figures stay half-sunk in their boxes with faces turned down. The call is real. I sense a reluctance to hear it, or a voice inside that keeps arguing the matter closed.",
"vision:major-21:up":"A dancer turns inside a great green wreath, a wand in each hand, a loose scarf drifting across the body. In the four corners, watchful faces look on. A circle is closing around your question, and it feels whole.",
"vision:major-21:rev":"The wreath still hangs there, but its ring is thin and the dancer moves slowly, looking back as if one small step is left undone. The ending is near, and the glass shows hesitation at the very last threshold.",
"vision:wands-01:up":"Out of a cloud, a hand offers a sturdy staff already sprouting green leaves. Far below, a castle waits on a hill and a river winds through quiet country. A spark of fresh energy is being handed to you, ready to grow.",
"vision:wands-01:rev":"The hand reaches from the cloud, but the staff held out is bare and the leaves fall away on the wind. A spark is offered here and it flickers. Nothing is lost, though the start wants more warmth before it catches.",
"vision:wands-02:up":"Alone on a castle wall, a figure in a rich red cap holds a small globe and leans on one staff, gazing over a bright sea. Another staff stands fixed beside them. Your question sits at a lookout, with wide choices below.",
"vision:wands-02:rev":"The figure on the wall has turned from the sea and stares at the parapet. The globe sits heavy in their palm and the horizon is dim. The plans exist, but fear of leaving the safe walls keeps the gate shut.",
"vision:wands-03:up":"A figure stands on a high cliff with their back to me, one hand on a staff, watching ships cross a golden sea. Two more staves are planted nearby. What you set in motion is already sailing out, and the view grows wider.",
"vision:wands-03:rev":"The ships are turning back toward the harbor, their sails slack, and the figure on the cliff shades their eyes against a haze. Efforts sent out are returning unfinished. Patience and a changed plan could send them out again.",
"vision:wands-04:up":"Four tall staves hold up a garland of flowers and fruit, and beyond it two figures raise bouquets in joy. A castle shines behind them and a crowd gathers. The glass fills with a homecoming, a settled and happy ground for your question.",
"vision:wands-04:rev":"The garland sags between its four poles and the party in the distance is quiet, half the guests already walking off. The gate to a home or a gathering stands open yet feels unfinished. Some steadiness has yet to be built.",
"vision:wands-05:up":"Five young people swing long staves at each other on bare ground, none in full agreement and none truly hurt. It is noisy, tangled and lively. Your question rests inside a contest of views, and the clash itself sharpens everyone.",
"vision:wands-05:rev":"The five staves are lowered or tangled, and the youths stand apart, glaring but not swinging. The quarrel has gone sour and quiet. Old rivalry hides under a polite surface and wants airing before it hardens.",
"vision:wands-06:up":"A rider in a laurel wreath sits tall on a white horse, a victory wreath tied to the staff held high, while the crowd below lifts their own staves in cheer. A public success rides through the glass, with every face turned toward you.",
"vision:wands-06:rev":"The rider still sits the white horse, but the road is empty and the crowd has thinned to a few turned backs. The wreath hangs crooked. Praise feels late or hollow, and the pride may need to wait for earned credit.",
"vision:wands-07:up":"High on a green hilltop, one figure grips a staff and fends off six others rising from below. One boot is odd and mismatched, yet the stance is firm. You hold a position in your question, and the higher ground is yours.",
"vision:wands-07:rev":"The figure on the hill lets the staff droop while the six below crowd closer, and the footing slips on loose earth. Too many demands press in at once. It may be wiser to choose which one fight is truly worth the effort.",
"vision:wands-08:up":"Eight long staves fly through a clear blue sky, all slanting the same way over a calm river and green hills. Nothing stands in their path. Your question carries a quick current: news, messages and movement arriving fast and in order.",
"vision:wands-08:rev":"The eight staves tumble in a tangle, some falling short, some crossing the others in mid-air under a clouded sky. Messages are crossed and plans arrive out of order. Slowing down and sorting the pieces would help before anything lands.",
"vision:wands-09:up":"A bandaged figure leans on a staff and glances over one shoulder, a row of eight staves standing like a fence behind. Tired, yet still on their feet. Your question has worn you, and I sense stamina left for one more watch.",
"vision:wands-09:rev":"The figure sags against the staff, head down, the bandage soaked, and the fence of staves behind them leans open. Weariness has grown into suspicion of everyone. Rest, and one honest request for help, would loosen it.",
"vision:wands-10:up":"A figure bent forward carries ten heavy staves bundled in both arms, trudging across a dusk field toward a village with lit windows. The home is close. Your question holds a load you chose, and the end of the road is in view.",
"vision:wands-10:rev":"The bundle of ten staves slips from the carrier's arms and several lie scattered on the path, while the village lights stay far off. More has been taken on than one pair of arms can hold. Setting a few down would speed the walk.",
"vision:wands-11:up":"A young figure in a patterned tunic stands in a golden desert, studying a leafy staff held upright, with pyramids small on the horizon. Curiosity is awake. A new message or a bold young idea is arriving in your question.",
"vision:wands-11:rev":"The young figure turns the staff over in their hands and looks away, and the desert wind blows the tunic's patterns into a blur. Enthusiasm starts and then stalls. The idea needs a firmer first step before it can be trusted.",
"vision:wands-12:up":"A mounted figure in armor rides a rearing chestnut horse across the sand, a staff raised, a plume streaming behind. Pyramids slide past in the heat. A fast, passionate energy charges into your question, eager to get moving.",
"vision:wands-12:rev":"The horse balks and turns in a circle, its rider tugging the reins and waving the staff at nothing. A great deal of heat, and no destination. Haste or a sudden mood may be scattering energy that wants a plan.",
"vision:wands-13:up":"A crowned figure sits on a lion-carved throne holding a blooming sunflower and a staff, a black cat at their feet and bright light on the hills. Warmth fills the glass. Your question is met with confidence and a welcoming fire.",
"vision:wands-13:rev":"The throne is the same, but the sunflower droops, the black cat has slunk to the shadow, and the seated figure looks sideways, jaw set. Confidence has turned prickly. Some jealousy or doubt wants to be named and let go.",
"vision:wands-14:up":"A crowned figure sits relaxed on a throne carved with lions and salamanders, a staff leaning in one hand and a calm gaze on the far side. Authority rests here without a shout. Your question meets steady, generous leadership.",
"vision:wands-14:rev":"The throne looks heavy now and the crowned figure grips the staff too hard, brow tight, the salamanders on the cloak coiled as if to snap. Leadership slides toward bossiness. Listening more could return the ease it lost.",
"vision:cups-01:up":"A hand rises from a cloud holding a golden cup, with five streams of water spilling into a pond of lilies below. A white dove drops a small wafer into the cup. Your question is being offered love, calm and an open heart.",
"vision:cups-01:rev":"The hand tips the cup and the water runs thin, splashing away unnoticed while the dove circles without landing. A gift of feeling is there, but it spills unused. Closing off or looking away leaves it going to waste.",
"vision:cups-02:up":"Two figures face each other and lift their cups in a quiet exchange, a winged lion's head glowing above them on a staff. Tenderness crosses the space between. Your question touches a true meeting, an equal give and take.",
"vision:cups-02:rev":"The two cups are raised, but the figures lean apart and the winged lion above them dims. Something between them is off balance: a hasty promise, a quiet silence, a lopsided effort. Honest talk would help to even the exchange.",
"vision:cups-03:up":"Three women in bright dresses lift their cups high in a circle, wreaths in their hair, with ripe fruit and gourds at their feet. Laughter rings. Your question finds friends, a feast and a shared joy that lifts every spirit.",
"vision:cups-03:rev":"The three raise their cups, but one has turned half away and the fruit at their feet lies unpicked. The party has cooled into cliques and whispers. Too much indulgence, or a friend left out, needs gentle attention.",
"vision:cups-04:up":"A figure sits under a tree with arms crossed and eyes on the ground, three cups lined up in front of them. From a cloud, a hand offers a fourth. Your question finds you looking inward, and a new gift waits, unnoticed.",
"vision:cups-04:rev":"The figure under the tree uncrosses their arms and lifts their eyes, and the cloud hand comes into focus. Boredom begins to lift. Yet the cups on the grass still sit untouched, so a first small step toward the offered one is needed.",
"vision:cups-05:up":"Mist parts on a cloaked figure in black, head bowed over three spilled cups. Behind the figure, a river runs past a distant house, and two cups still stand upright, unnoticed. Your question is wrapped in what was lost.",
"vision:cups-05:rev":"The dark cloak loosens, and the bowed figure begins to turn from the spilled cups. A thin light falls on the two that remained standing. Grief has been carried long enough, and the glass shows the first small movement toward what is left.",
"vision:cups-06:up":"A sunlit courtyard opens in the glass, where one small child offers another a cup full of flowers. Old plastered walls and a quiet village frame them. Something tender from the past, a memory or an old kindness, bears on your question.",
"vision:cups-06:rev":"The courtyard looks faded, as if seen through a window clouded by years. The flowers in the cups lean toward a past that cannot be handed back. The glass hints that your question asks you to stop living in an old garden and step out of its gate.",
"vision:cups-07:up":"A shadowed figure stands before a cloud, and seven cups float in the haze. Each holds a different wonder: jewels, a castle, a laurel wreath, a coiled snake, a dragon. The glass warns that so many glittering choices blur together before your question.",
"vision:cups-07:rev":"The floating cups sharpen and drift closer, their wonders losing their glitter. The figure steps back from the haze and looks at each one plainly. Daydreams are thinning, and a single honest choice begins to stand out in the glass.",
"vision:cups-08:up":"Under a pale moon with a shadowed face, a figure in a red cloak walks away from eight neatly stacked cups. A staff is in hand, and dark hills rise ahead. I see someone leaving what looks complete because it no longer feeds the heart.",
"vision:cups-08:rev":"The figure in the red cloak lingers at the stacked cups, one foot raised but not yet set down. The hills ahead stay faint in the night. The glass shows a departure delayed, or a restless wandering with no clear road under it.",
"vision:cups-09:up":"A contented figure sits on a bench, arms folded, red cap tilted, with nine golden cups arranged on a curved shelf behind. A warm blue cloth hangs there. Your question meets a wish that is close to granted, and the glass glows with plain satisfaction.",
"vision:cups-09:rev":"The golden cups on the shelf look polished but a little hollow, and the figure on the bench stares past them with folded arms. Something about the wish feels too easy or too showy. The glass asks what would actually satisfy you.",
"vision:cups-10:up":"Beneath a rainbow of ten bright cups, two figures stand with arms lifted toward each other and the sky. Two children dance beside them, and a little house waits beyond a river. Your question settles into belonging and ordinary joy.",
"vision:cups-10:rev":"The rainbow of cups hangs dim above a house with its shutters closed. The family figures stand a little apart, arms lowered. The glass shows a harmony that is staged or strained, and something quiet that needs saying before warmth can return.",
"vision:cups-11:up":"A young figure in a flowered tunic and soft blue hat stands by the sea, holding a cup. From the cup a small fish leaps and gazes up. A playful message surfaces in the glass, odd and sweet, and it touches your question.",
"vision:cups-11:rev":"The young figure holds the cup close, and the fish inside has gone still. The waves behind them look restless and a little sulky. A tender feeling stays unspoken in the glass, or a mood is being indulged more than shared.",
"vision:cups-12:up":"A rider on a white horse advances slowly beside a calm river, a winged helmet on their head and a cup held out in front. Distant mountains sit quietly behind. An invitation arrives gently, carrying an open heart to your question.",
"vision:cups-12:rev":"The white horse stands still at the water's edge, and the rider's cup tilts, half forgotten. Winged ornaments gleam, but the road ahead goes nowhere. The glass shows charm without follow-through, or a promise that sounds better than it moves.",
"vision:cups-13:up":"A calm figure sits on a carved throne at the edge of the sea, gazing into an ornate covered cup. Waves lap at the base of it. I see deep feeling held steady, and a quiet knowing that serves your question well.",
"vision:cups-13:rev":"The tide has risen to the throne, and the covered cup trembles in two hands. The figure's gaze goes inward, drifting. The glass shows a heart soaked in other people's moods, and your question wants firmer ground beneath it.",
"vision:cups-14:up":"A figure in blue sits on a throne that floats on a restless sea, a cup in one hand and a scepter in the other. A fish leaps and a ship passes behind. Feeling and clear judgment sit together in the glass, answering your question calmly.",
"vision:cups-14:rev":"Waves slap hard against the floating throne, and the cup tips toward the water. The figure holds the scepter tightly but looks away from the sea. The glass shows feelings pressed down until they leak out sideways, shadowing your question.",
"vision:swords-01:up":"A hand reaches from a cloud and grips a single upright sword, its point wearing a golden crown with laurel and palm. Bare mountains rise below. The glass cuts clean through fog, giving your question a sudden, honest clarity.",
"vision:swords-01:rev":"The hand from the cloud grips the sword unsteadily, and the crown on its tip tilts. Mist crowds the bare peaks below. A thought is too sharp or not yet formed, and the glass suggests waiting before you speak it.",
"vision:swords-02:up":"A blindfolded figure sits on a plain bench by a moonlit sea, arms crossed, holding two swords balanced against each other. Behind them, rocks break the still water. A choice hangs in the glass, and your question is held in careful stillness.",
"vision:swords-02:rev":"The blindfold slips and the crossed swords wobble. Waves behind the bench grow rough, and the figure shifts uneasily. The stalemate in the glass cannot hold much longer, and your question wants the uncomfortable truth let in.",
"vision:swords-03:up":"Under heavy grey clouds and falling rain, a red heart hangs in the air, pierced by three swords. Nothing else is in the scene. The glass shows a plain, honest ache, the kind that comes with your question when something true is finally named.",
"vision:swords-03:rev":"The rain thins, and the three swords begin to slide from the red heart. Grey clouds break at one edge. Old hurt is releasing slowly in the glass, though it may linger if held too tightly, and your question rests inside that slow easing.",
"vision:swords-04:up":"In a hushed chapel, a carved figure lies on a tomb, hands pressed together. Three swords hang on the wall above, and one rests beneath. Coloured light falls from a high window. Your question asks for deliberate rest.",
"vision:swords-04:rev":"The carved figure on the tomb seems to stir, and the swords on the wall gleam faintly. Coloured light from the window creeps across the floor. Rest has gone on long enough or never came at all, and the glass nudges you toward the next step.",
"vision:swords-05:up":"A figure with a smirk gathers three swords while two others lie on the ground. At the shore, two figures walk off with heads lowered under a stormy sky. A win in the glass carries a cost, and your question asks whether it was worth it.",
"vision:swords-05:rev":"The figure holding the swords looks less certain, and the wind drags at the scene. Those who walked away turn at the water's edge to look back. The quarrel in the glass is spent, and your question wants peace more than victory.",
"vision:swords-06:up":"A boatman poles a small ferry across grey water. A cloaked figure and a child sit hunched aboard, six swords standing upright in the hull. Ahead the water is smooth. A passage toward calmer ground opens in the glass for your question.",
"vision:swords-06:rev":"The ferry drifts in choppy water, and the boatman leans heavily on the pole. The six swords rattle in the hull and the far shore stays faint. The glass shows a move that is stalled or half made, with something unfinished still aboard.",
"vision:swords-07:up":"A figure tiptoes away from a row of tents at dusk, carrying five swords and glancing back. Two blades are left standing in the ground. A clever plan is at work in the glass, and your question asks what is being taken or hidden.",
"vision:swords-07:rev":"The figure stops short of the tents and sets the swords back in the dirt. Behind them, a lantern flickers on. In the glass a scheme is dropped or uncovered, and honesty feels easier than the sneaking did for your question.",
"vision:swords-08:up":"A figure stands in a shallow pool, blindfolded and loosely bound, ringed by eight upright swords. A castle sits on a far hill. The glass shows a cage with gaps in it, one your own thinking helped build around your question.",
"vision:swords-08:rev":"The loose bindings begin to slip, and the blindfold lifts a little. Eight swords still stand but now they leave a visible path out of the pool. A freedom is dawning in the glass, and the first steps toward it are your own.",
"vision:swords-09:up":"In a dark room, a figure sits bolt upright in bed, face buried in both hands. Nine swords hang in the black above, over a quilt stitched with roses. Sleepless worry fills the glass, and your question is tangled in it.",
"vision:swords-09:rev":"The nine swords on the wall fade a shade, and a pale hint of morning edges the dark room. The figure in bed lifts their face from their hands. In the glass, worry is easing, though it still wants words spoken to someone you trust.",
"vision:swords-10:up":"A figure lies face down on dark ground, ten swords across their back, as black clouds hang above still water. Along the horizon, gold light is rising. The glass shows an ending that is complete and over, and your question stands at the edge of dawn.",
"vision:swords-10:rev":"The ten swords loosen, and the figure begins to push up from the dark ground. The golden horizon grows wider and the black sky thins. The glass shows the worst already passing, though the rising is slow, and your question wants patience with it.",
"vision:swords-11:up":"A young figure stands on a windy green hill, a bright blade raised in both hands. Clouds boil overhead and birds scatter, but the gaze stays sharp and curious. Something in your question wants to be asked out loud.",
"vision:swords-11:rev":"On the same windswept hill, the blade dips and wavers while the young watcher glances in three directions at once. Sharp words fly loose in the gale. Your question needs a slower, steadier aim before anyone speaks.",
"vision:swords-12:up":"A rider in bright armor charges across the glass at full gallop, blade lifted, trees bent flat behind and clouds torn into streamers. Speed and certainty fill the scene. Your question is moving fast, and clear thinking is driving it.",
"vision:swords-12:rev":"The galloping rider in armor reins in too late, horse skidding, blade swinging wild while the storm pushes the trees sideways. Haste has outrun the plan. Your question may need a breath before the next charge.",
"vision:swords-13:up":"A calm figure sits on a high carved seat, one hand raised, a sword held straight beside a clear sky and thin clouds. The air is cold and honest. Your question is asking for plain truth, spoken without fuss.",
"vision:swords-13:rev":"The seat on the high ground stands in shadow now, the raised hand trembling and the sword tilted toward dark clouds. The seated figure is holding back a lot of old hurt. Your question may be sharpened by that coldness.",
"vision:swords-14:up":"A crowned ruler sits on a throne carved with butterflies, a blade upright, the sky pale and still. Judgment settles over the scene like clear water. Your question is best met with fairness and evidence.",
"vision:swords-14:rev":"The throne carved with butterflies sits cold, and the crowned ruler grips the blade too tightly, gaze fixed on nothing warm. A harsh verdict hangs in the air. Your question needs reason, but also a softer hand.",
"vision:pentacles-01:up":"A hand reaches out of a cloud and offers a golden coin that glows above a garden gate, lilies and an arch of leaves beyond. A path leads through toward distant mountains. Your question holds a real, usable beginning.",
"vision:pentacles-01:rev":"The hand from the cloud holds out its golden coin, but the garden path beyond looks overgrown and the gate half shut. The offer is there, only not yet ready. Your question needs patient groundwork first.",
"vision:pentacles-02:up":"A cheerful figure in a red cap dances on a sandy shore, juggling two coins linked by a looping ribbon while ships ride great green swells behind. Balance is being kept in motion. Your question asks for light, steady footing.",
"vision:pentacles-02:rev":"The juggler in the red cap lurches as the ribbon tangles, one coin slipping while waves heave the ships behind. Too many things are in the air at once. Your question needs fewer balls to keep spinning.",
"vision:pentacles-03:up":"Inside a vaulted church, a craftsperson stands on a bench carving an arch while two others hold up plans and speak low. Light falls on the work. Your question grows best through skill and teamwork.",
"vision:pentacles-03:rev":"In the vaulted church the carver works alone on the bench while two onlookers argue over rolled plans and never meet the other's eye. The arch sits half-shaped. Your question needs a shared vision and honest feedback.",
"vision:pentacles-04:up":"A crowned figure sits on a plain bench before a small city, one coin balanced on the head, one held tight to the chest, two more beneath the feet. Holding firm feels like safety. Your question touches security and what you guard.",
"vision:pentacles-04:rev":"The seated figure before the small city loosens a grip, and a coin slides from the chest to roll across the ground. Something once clutched begins to move. Your question asks what you can safely let go.",
"vision:pentacles-05:up":"Two ragged figures trudge through falling snow past a lit church window, one on crutches, bandaged and bowing against the cold. The glow is close, though neither looks up. Your question hides a door that is open if you ask.",
"vision:pentacles-05:rev":"The snow thins over the two weary travelers, and the lit window of the church warms into view. One lifts a head toward the glow. Your question is nearing shelter, if you let help be offered.",
"vision:pentacles-06:up":"A well-dressed merchant holds scales in one hand and drops coins into the palms of two kneeling beggars. The scene is quiet and measured. Your question turns on giving and receiving in fair proportion.",
"vision:pentacles-06:rev":"The merchant with the scales tips the balance, one beggar's hand left empty while another receives more than needed. Strings seem tied to the coins. Your question asks whether the exchange is truly even.",
"vision:pentacles-07:up":"A farmer leans on a hoe beside a thick green bush hung with round coins, gazing at the fruit with calm patience. The work is done, the harvest still ripening. Your question rewards steady waiting and a clear look.",
"vision:pentacles-07:rev":"The farmer at the bush turns away from the hoe, shoulders slumped, while the coins hang less full than hoped. Effort feels wasted. Your question needs a review of the work and some patience.",
"vision:pentacles-08:up":"A craftsperson sits at a bench in a quiet workshop, hammer and chisel in hand, tapping a coin-shaped design onto a row of finished pieces. Focus is complete. Your question is best met by practice and careful detail.",
"vision:pentacles-08:rev":"At the workbench, the craftsperson's chisel slips and the pieces stand uneven while the tools lie scattered. Attention drifts. Your question calls for slowing down, or for finding the work worth caring about again.",
"vision:pentacles-09:up":"A poised figure in an embroidered gown stands in a vineyard heavy with grapes, a hooded falcon on a gloved hand and a snail on the ground. Everything here was earned slowly. Your question points to quiet comfort made by your own effort.",
"vision:pentacles-09:rev":"In the heavy vineyard the poised figure stands alone, the falcon restless on the glove and the gate far down the path. Comfort feels hollow without company. Your question asks what the work has really been for.",
"vision:pentacles-10:up":"Beneath a tall arch, an old man sits with two dogs while a couple and a child stand nearby, a castle rising behind them in warm light. Several generations share one place. Your question touches lasting roots and belonging.",
"vision:pentacles-10:rev":"The tall arch looms over the family and the castle, and the old man's gaze turns inward while the dogs fidget. Old arrangements feel heavy. Your question asks which inheritances you want to keep and which to set down.",
"vision:pentacles-11:up":"A young figure stands in a green meadow, studying a single golden coin held up in both hands, fresh ploughed earth and distant hills behind. Curiosity is quiet and patient. Your question invites careful learning.",
"vision:pentacles-11:rev":"In the meadow the young figure stares at the coin and misses the field's wide path, one boot half out of the furrow. Daydreams outrun the work. Your question needs a small, practical first step.",
"vision:pentacles-12:up":"A rider on a heavy black horse sits perfectly still in a ploughed field, holding a coin and watching the soil. Nothing rushes. Your question is served by reliability and slow, honest progress.",
"vision:pentacles-12:rev":"The rider on the heavy black horse is stuck in the furrows, the horse planted, the coin gripped tight. Caution has hardened into standing still. Your question may need a small change of routine.",
"vision:pentacles-13:up":"A seated figure in a flowering garden cradles a large golden coin in the lap, a rabbit near the skirt and roses climbing overhead. Care and plenty feel natural here. Your question is held in a warm, practical hand.",
"vision:pentacles-13:rev":"In the flowering garden the seated figure holds the coin with a distracted look, weeds creeping up beside the rabbit and roses. Care has been stretched thin. Your question asks for attention to your own needs too.",
"vision:pentacles-14:up":"A bearded ruler on a throne carved with bulls and vines holds a scepter and a coin, a castle and grape-hung garden around. Prosperity looks steady and built to last. Your question favors solid, generous leadership.",
"vision:pentacles-14:rev":"The throne of bulls and vines creaks as the ruler grips the scepter and coin, gaze fixed on the castle walls. Holding on matters more than enjoying. Your question asks whether the wealth is serving you.",
"cb:yes:1":"The glass warms and brightens, and the light inside it leans toward yes, though the final step is still yours to take.",
"cb:yes:2":"Silver clouds drift apart, and the first thing the ball shows me tilts gently toward yes.",
"cb:yes:3":"A steady glow gathers at the center of the ball, and it points more toward yes than away from it.",
"cb:yes:4":"Look how clear the glass has turned. The pictures inside it lean toward yes, and I will tell you what they hold.",
"cb:no:1":"The glass cools and dims a little, and the pictures in it lean toward no, though nothing in it is fixed.",
"cb:no:2":"Shadows settle low in the ball, and its first answer leans toward no. Listen to why before you decide what to make of it.",
"cb:no:3":"A pale hush crosses the ball, and the weight of what I see tips toward no for now.",
"cb:no:4":"The light inside the glass turns away from your question, leaning toward no. Let me show you what it shows instead.",
"cb:mixed:1":"The glass flickers between light and shade, so the answer is a qualified one: yes in some ways, not yet in others.",
"cb:mixed:2":"Two currents swirl inside the ball and neither wins outright, which tells me the answer depends on conditions you can still shape.",
"cb:mixed:3":"Half the ball glows and half stays dim, so your question has a divided answer, and the details matter here.",
"cb:mixed:4":"Neither yes nor no settles in the glass. It offers a maybe with strings attached, and the pictures explain the strings.",
"cb:open:1":"The mists inside the ball begin to thin, and your question opens like a window onto a wide landscape.",
"cb:open:2":"Slowly the fog lifts from the glass, and pictures rise through it to answer what you have asked.",
"cb:open:3":"Color seeps into the clouded ball, and shapes start to form as your question settles into focus.",
"cb:open:4":"The ball clears like a morning sky after rain, and scenes gather within it to speak to your question.",
"cb:close:1":"The glass clouds over again and the pictures fade, leaving the road ahead as open as it was when you arrived.",
"cb:close:2":"Slowly the light sinks out of the ball. What it showed is a possibility, and the choosing is still in your hands.",
"cb:close:3":"The mist returns and the scenes soften into silver. Carry what rang true and set down the rest.",
"cb:close:4":"The ball goes quiet now. Nothing it showed is fixed, and your next decision can still bend the story.",
"cb:close:5":"The last glimmer slips from the glass. Whatever comes next begins with what you choose to do tomorrow.",
"cb:close:6":"The ball darkens to a calm, clear surface once more, and the future in it is as unwritten as a blank page.",
"cb:close:7":"The vision melts into the mist like breath on a window. You leave with a picture to think about, not a verdict.",
"cb:close:8":"The glow retreats and the glass rests. Hold the images lightly, because the path forward is shaped by your steps.",
"geo:Via":"A road with no fences. Via is the figure of movement, ruled by the Moon, and it says that nothing in your question is meant to stay where it is. It suits journeys, moves, job changes and any matter that needs to get going. It is a poor sign for anything that depends on staying put, such as a lease you hope to keep. Picture the friend who is always halfway out the door with a packed bag: wonderful for a trip, tiring for a quiet evening. The advice is to follow the motion rather than fight it, and to keep your plans light enough to change.",
"geo:Populus":"A crowd gathering in a square. Populus is the figure of the many, ruled by the Moon, and it behaves like a mirror: it takes on the character of whatever figures sit near it. Alone it is passive and neutral, neither pushing a matter forward nor blocking it. In an everyday situation it points to the group, the neighborhood, the office, or the opinion of everyone around you. Think of a restaurant that is full because other people chose it. The advice is to look at what surrounds your question, because the surroundings carry more weight than any single choice you make.",
"geo:Conjunctio":"Two hands joining. Conjunctio is the figure of meeting, ruled by Mercury, and it speaks of things coming together: people, ideas, agreements, even lost objects found again. It is favorable for reunions, partnerships, negotiation and anything that needs to be reconnected. It can also mean being tied to a mix of people or messages that does not quite sort itself out. Picture a mutual friend who introduces two people who turn out to need each other. The advice is to make the call, send the message, and say plainly what you are hoping the other side can bring.",
"geo:Carcer":"A locked room with a small window. Carcer is the figure of binding, ruled by Saturn, and it describes restriction, delay, and a sense of being held in place. For most questions it is a hard answer, since it slows things down and closes doors. It is a good sign only when you want something to stay fixed, such as a secret kept, a boundary held, or a structure that must not move. Think of a project stuck in approvals while a fence quietly keeps the dog safe. The advice is patience, and a clear look at which limits protect you.",
"geo:FortunaMajor":"A sturdy tower with its own fire lit. Fortuna Major is the figure of greater fortune, ruled by the Sun, and it points to success that grows from your own steady effort. It carries strength, protection and standing, and it favors long projects that need a firm base. It is less about luck falling from the sky and more about work that has been quietly adding up. Picture the person whose small daily habits finally make a hard task look easy. The advice is to keep going at the same patient pace and to accept the support others offer along the way.",
"geo:FortunaMinor":"A gust of wind at your back. Fortuna Minor is the figure of lesser fortune, ruled by the Sun, and it suggests help that arrives quickly from outside you, but does not always last. It is excellent when speed matters: a fast reply, a quick favor, a short task done before a deadline. It is weaker for building something that has to stand for years. Imagine a neighbor who lends a ladder the moment you ask, though the ladder goes back tomorrow. The advice is to use the help while it is here, and to plan your own footing for afterward.",
"geo:Acquisitio":"Open hands receiving. Acquisitio is the figure of gain, ruled by Jupiter, and it points toward getting what you are seeking: an answer, an offer, a skill, a favorable result. It is a generous sign for most questions, especially those about obtaining something you have worked toward. It asks only that you stay clear about what you actually want, because it tends to deliver the thing you named. Picture someone who finally gets the reply they wrote for. The advice is to ask directly, hold your aim steady, and be as specific as you can about the result.",
"geo:Amissio":"A hand opening and letting go. Amissio is the figure of loss, ruled by Venus, and it describes things slipping away: possessions, habits, attention, sometimes a connection that has run its course. For most questions it is unwelcome, since it speaks of what drains out. It is a good sign only when your question is about being rid of something, such as clutter, a burden, or a pattern that no longer serves you. Think of clearing out a closet and feeling lighter. The advice is to decide what you truly want to keep, and let the rest go without fuss.",
"geo:Laetitia":"A face turned up toward morning light. Laetitia is the figure of joy, ruled by Jupiter, and it carries a rising, hopeful mood. It points to good spirits, welcome news, recovery of confidence, and a matter that lifts as it moves. It favors anything that depends on morale, such as teamwork, celebrations, or a fresh start after a heavy stretch. It can also make you overlook small details because the mood is so pleasant. Picture a long dinner where everyone leaves happier than they arrived. The advice is to enjoy the lift and still read the fine print.",
"geo:Tristitia":"A well dug deep into the ground. Tristitia is the figure of sorrow, ruled by Saturn, and it points downward: weight, heaviness, withdrawal, and slow going. For most questions it is a difficult figure, since it dims the mood and holds things low. Its gift is solidity, so it suits foundations, digging in, and anything meant to be built to last. Think of a quiet season when you do the unglamorous groundwork that later makes everything steadier. The advice is to be gentle with yourself, move slowly, and trust that depth can be a place to build from.",
"geo:Puella":"A mirror held in a gentle hand. Puella is the figure of the girl, ruled by Venus, and it speaks of harmony, beauty, pleasure and kindness. It suits matters of affection, art, hospitality and anything that needs a softer touch. Its weak side is being changeable, pleasing everyone and settling on nothing. Picture the person who makes a room feel welcoming but cannot decide what to order. The advice is to lead with warmth and courtesy, and to anchor your question with one clear choice so the charm does not drift into indecision.",
"geo:Puer":"A young warrior with a raised hand. Puer is the figure of the boy, ruled by Mars, and it brings raw energy, courage and speed. It suits contests, competition, bold starts and anything that needs nerve. It can also be rash, acting before the facts are in. Think of the driver who leaps at a gap in traffic and either saves ten minutes or earns a scare. The advice is to use the fire on purpose: pick one target, act with confidence, and slow down for a breath before you press send on something you cannot take back.",
"geo:Rubeus":"A flushed face and a clenched jaw. Rubeus is the figure of red, ruled by Mars, and it speaks of heated feeling: passion, anger, appetite, and the urge to react right now. For most questions it is a warning to pause, since decisions made in this heat tend to burn. It is not wicked, only loud. Picture the email typed in a rage that reads very differently the next morning. The advice is to cool the situation before you move, let the strong feeling pass through your body, and return to the question once your head is clear again.",
"geo:Albus":"Clear water in a still bowl. Albus is the figure of white, ruled by Mercury, and it points to peace, clear thinking and wisdom that comes with time. It favors calm negotiation, study, careful planning and any matter that rewards patience. It does not rush, and good results tend to arrive slowly. Picture someone who listens fully before answering and ends up saying exactly the right thing. The advice is to keep your mind level, gather what you need to know, and let the matter settle into its proper shape instead of forcing a quick finish.",
"geo:CaputDraconis":"A door swinging open on a new hall. Caput Draconis is the Dragon's Head, ruled by the North Node, and it marks the start of something: first steps, invitations, fresh chances. It is a good figure for beginnings and a poor one for finishing, since its energy is all about entering. It also tends to magnify whatever figures sit near it. Think of the first day at a new place, before anything has gone wrong or right. The advice is to step in now, set the early tone with care, and expect the middle of the journey to need its own energy.",
"geo:CaudaDraconis":"A gate closing softly behind you. Cauda Draconis is the Dragon's Tail, ruled by the South Node, and it speaks of endings, exits and release. For new ventures it is a poor sign, since its movement runs outward and backward. It is good for finishing, clearing, concluding and leaving what is done behind. Picture packing the last box before a move, tired but relieved. The advice is to close what needs closing, thank what has served its purpose, and avoid starting something large while the energy is still pointed toward the exit.",
"geojudge:Via":"Final answer: a road, still being walked. The result is on the move and was never meant to be settled. It leans toward change, travel, a shift of place or plans. That is welcome if your question wants movement and less welcome if you wanted stability. Read the answer as an open road rather than a closed door, expect adjustments, and stay flexible. The tone is neither good nor bad, only restless, and it asks you to travel light.",
"geojudge:Populus":"Final answer: a crowd, and it follows the current. This Judge does not push hard toward yes or no, so the result depends on the figures around it and on the people involved in your question. The tone is neutral and a little passive. Look at what the other houses say, and at the mood of those around you. The answer is to wait and watch, since the matter will follow the general flow rather than choose a path alone.",
"geojudge:Conjunctio":"Final answer: a meeting. Conjunctio in the Judge's seat says the matter turns on connection, and the answer leans toward things coming together, whether people, pieces of information or something mislaid that turns up again. The tone is mixed, since joining can be a help or a tangle depending on who is joined. Think of two roads merging into one. Read the answer as a nudge to reach out, ask for the conversation, and check carefully who or what you are being tied to.",
"geojudge:Carcer":"Judged by the Prison, your question meets a closed door. The answer leans toward delay, restriction and a sense of being held. It is not a verdict on you, only on the current conditions, which are tight and slow. The one exception is a question about keeping something safe or fixed, where this figure is a friend. Think of a gate that stays shut until the right key arrives. Use the pause to prepare, trim what is unnecessary, and test which limits are worth keeping.",
"geojudge:FortunaMajor":"Greater Fortune sits in the Judge's seat, and the answer leans warmly toward success that lasts. The tone is good and sturdy: the result is likely to hold because it rests on your own effort and steady support. It is no promise, only a strong lean. Picture a house with a solid foundation that others are glad to stand near. Take the answer as encouragement to keep doing the patient, ordinary work that has brought you this far, and to accept help when it is offered.",
"geojudge:FortunaMinor":"Lesser Fortune, as the final figure, gives a quick and friendly answer. It leans toward help arriving from outside, and toward results that come fast. The tone is good, with one caution: the lift may not stay for long. Imagine catching a ride that takes you most of the way. The answer rewards speed, so act promptly and gratefully, and then arrange your own way of covering the remaining distance once the helpful wind has passed.",
"geojudge:Acquisitio":"Gain stands as the final answer, and it leans toward getting what you are seeking. The tone is good and open-handed: your question points toward receiving, obtaining, or reaching the thing you named. It is a lean, not a guarantee. Picture a table being set for you. Read the answer as permission to ask clearly and to state exactly what you want, since this figure tends to hand over what it is asked for, in the form you described.",
"geojudge:Amissio":"Loss closes the reading, and the answer leans toward something slipping away. The tone is poor for questions about keeping or gaining, and favorable for questions about letting go. Your wording of the question decides which. Think of a tide pulling a tangle of seaweed off the shore. If you hoped to hold on, take the answer as a prompt to look at what you can protect now. If you hoped to be free of it, the figure agrees with you.",
"geoperf:occupation":"The same figure sits in the place for you and in the place for the matter, so the two literally stand in the same spot. It reads as a direct, strong coming-together that needs no go-between. Think of two people arriving at the same doorway at the same minute. The matter and the person asking are aligned, and this is among the clearest signs that the thing you seek is within reach.",
"geoperf:conjunction":"Neighboring houses hold the figures of you and the matter, and they lean toward each other. You and the matter are close and moving in each other's direction, though not yet touching. It reads as steady approach rather than sudden arrival. Picture two walkers on a path who can see each other across a field. The advice is to keep the movement going: small steps, regular contact, and no big leaps.",
"geoperf:mutation":"The figures of you and the matter sit side by side somewhere else in the chart, in a place neither started from. They meet, but by an unexpected route, and not the way you pictured. Think of two friends who run into each other at a different event from the one planned. The advice is to stay open about the how. The meeting is possible, yet it comes through a side door.",
"geoperf:translation":"One figure sits next to both you and the matter, acting as a go-between. A third person, event or circumstance carries a message from one side to the other and brings them together. Picture the mutual friend who happens to know both parties. The advice is to notice who or what sits between you and what you seek, and to treat that link kindly. The result depends on this middle point.",
"geoperf:none":"The figures of you and the matter never meet by any of the four routes. They stay apart in the chart, so the usual road to a match does not open here. This describes this moment and not a verdict on your life. Picture two rivers in parallel valleys. The advice is to ask the question differently, wait for conditions to change, or check whether the matter is what you truly need.",
"geoans:good:perf":"The answer leans clearly toward yes. The Judge is favorable and the matter comes together by a real route, so tone and mechanics point the same way. Nothing is certain, but conditions look supportive. Move forward calmly, say what you want clearly, and keep your own effort in the picture.",
"geoans:good:none":"The tone is friendly, but the matter does not come together by the usual route. The Judge speaks well of the situation, yet you and the thing sought stay apart in the chart. Read it as goodwill without a direct path for now. Keep your hope, and look for a different way in.",
"geoans:mixed:perf":"The answer is a qualified yes. The matter comes together, but the Judge is mixed, so it arrives with changes, extra people or conditions attached. Expect the outcome to differ a little from the picture in your mind. Stay flexible, keep your questions practical, and accept that some trade-offs come with getting there.",
"geoans:mixed:none":"The answer is unsettled. The Judge is mixed and the matter does not come together by this route, so the chart shows neither a clear push nor a clear block. Think of a fork in the road with no sign. Gather information, wait for the situation to move, and revisit the question when something shifts.",
"geoans:bad:perf":"The matter comes together, but the Judge is unfavorable, so the result may arrive with a cost or a rough edge. It is a chance that needs careful handling. Nothing is fixed, and your choices still count. Read the terms, ask what you are agreeing to, and move at a pace that lets you step back.",
"geoans:bad:none":"The answer leans toward no. The Judge is unfavorable and the matter does not come together, so both signs point away from the result you hoped for. This reads present conditions only, and conditions can change. Consider it a polite closed door. Redirect your effort to something with more support."};
